"erick713006", "id": 168612416, "node_id": "U_kgDOCgzSQA", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/168612416?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/erick713006", "html_url": "https://github.com/erick713006", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/erick713006/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/erick713006/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/erick713006/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/erick713006/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/erick713006/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/erick713006/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/erick713006/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/erick713006/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/erick713006/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "created_at": "2026-08-12T19:00:19Z", "updated_at": "2026-08-13T20:35:44Z", "body": "### Split diagnosis (dirname warning vs real failure)\n\nYour log shows two different things:\n\n1. **Cosmetics / noise (not the exit 1)**  \n   ```\n   Your Vite config uses features that are unsupported by `configLoader: 'native'`\n   - `__dirname` (vite.config.ts:\u2026). Use `import.meta.dirname` instead\n   ```\n   That warning is still on main. Same class as #76207 / #79664. I fixed the ESM dirname usage across the affected Vite configs in **https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent/pull/78131** (single commit; web uses `fileURLToPath`; the others use `import.meta.dirname`; no `engines.npm` floor change).\n\n2. **Actual failure**  \n   ```\n   Error: [stage-native-deps] get-windows has no win32 prebuilt binding under lib/binding\n   \u2026\n   apps/desktop build failed (exit 1)\n   ```\n   That is a **desktop native-deps / get-windows** packaging problem, not the Vite dirname warning. #78131 does **not** claim to fix this desktop stage failure.\n\nSo: the yellow Vite warning is the known dashboard/desktop config issue tracked above; the blocker for update/reinstall here is the `get-windows` prebuild stage.\n", "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR", "pin": null, "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/NousResearch/hermes-agent/issues/comments/5271403389/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "performed_via_github_app": null, "minimized": null}, {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/NousResearch/hermes-agent/issues/comments/5300465545", "html_url": "https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent/issues/82168#issuecomment-5300465545", "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/NousResearch/hermes-agent/issues/82168", "id": 5300465545, "node_id": "IC_kwDOPRF1G88AAAABO-6viQ", "user": {"login": "teknium1", "id": 127238744, "node_id": "U_kgDOB5WCWA", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/127238744?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/teknium1", "html_url": "https://github.com/teknium1", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/teknium1/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/teknium1/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/teknium1/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/teknium1/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/teknium1/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/teknium1/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/teknium1/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/teknium1/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/teknium1/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "created_at": "2026-08-15T04:10:46Z", "updated_at": "2026-08-15T04:10:46Z", "body": "Triage complete \u2014 this is fixed on `main`; please update again.\n\nSplitting your log per @erick713006's diagnosis (which is exactly right):\n\n1. **The actual failure** \u2014 `[stage-native-deps] get-windows has no win32 prebuilt binding under lib/binding` \u2192 `apps/desktop build failed (exit 1)`. Your bootstrap ran at 2026-08-09 02:03 UTC. The fix landed on main **twenty minutes later**: commit `2cd9e1777b` (\"fix(desktop): rebuild get-windows when its win32 binding is missing\", 2026-08-09 02:23 UTC) makes the staging script run `npm rebuild get-windows` automatically when the prebuilt binding is absent (the state a blocked/skipped install script leaves behind), instead of throwing. Follow-ups hardened this further: `58e4bb04d6` made get-windows an optional dependency and `689a4be6f2`/`a373a1b749` degrade gracefully when it can't be built (ARM64). So current main either rebuilds the binding or tolerates its absence \u2014 the hard failure you hit can no longer abort the desktop stage.\n2. **The Vite `__dirname` warning** \u2014 cosmetic noise, unrelated to the exit 1, tracked in #76207/#79664 with a fix in flight (#78131).\n\n**What to do:** run the installer again (or `hermes update --yes` from a terminal) \u2014 you'll pull a checkout with the fixed staging script. If the desktop stage still fails on a current checkout, please attach `%TEMP%\\hermes-desktop-build-*.log` plus a fresh `logs.zip` (`hermes debug share`) and we'll reopen.\n\nClosing as fixed on main (credit: the `2cd9e1777b` staging fallback and @erick713006's split diagnosis). Comment here if it reproduces on \u2265 v0.20.1 and we'll reopen.\n", "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR", "pin": null, "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/NousResearch/hermes-agent/issues/comments/5300465545/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "performed_via_github_app": null, "minimized": null}]